 "note": "Freeze protocol (two stages, decided before any report-bank prompt was rendered): stage 1 freezes everything — architecture, L_max 256, data sources and splits, mixture 70/30, 100k prompts (1,563 x 64), optimizer and learning rates, 24,576-token LLaDA microbatches, final-checkpoint rule, tokenizer revisions, batching, sampling, seeds — plus the LLaDA and Nemotron checkpoints (both development-checked). dQwen's training run had already started with the identical frozen config; its checkpoint hash is appended by `lpx_freeze.py --complete` only after the run ends and only if `runs/<run>/config.json` is byte-identical (SHA-256 recorded here). No report-bank result of any backbone can change any frozen item; a failed dQwen development check would be reported, not fixed.\nReport K: K = 64 / J proposals per family (J = 1, 2, 4, 8 -> K = 64, 32, 16, 8), i.e. 64 sampled targets per family in every cell; a compute-driven deviation from K = 64 at every J (per-candidate canvases rarely share a length, so J = 8 at K = 64 would cost ~8 GPU-hours per backbone on the shared GPUs). The oracle condition is the Section-4.2 K = 64 pool of the same families (bit-identical reproduction verified for LLaDA and Nemotron; dQwen drift caveat in DQWEN_PORT.md, plus a same-session dQwen delta-0 rerun at J = 1, 2).\nGeneration-path code (dr_worker.py, mm_common.py, mm_adapters.py, lpx_model.py, lpx_alloc.py, lpx_train.py) is frozen at the hashes below; analysis / plotting scripts may receive documented fixes afterwards.",
